[wait time="0.2"]
join Lizzy righter [animation="Slide From Right" length="1.0"]
VO: That was even worse than last time.
update Barb [animation="Bounce" length="0.3" repeat="3"]
Barb: Finally, we’ve been waiting here for eons.
[wait time="0.2"]
update Juniper [mirrored="false"]
Juniper: Barb’s just being mean because she’s excited.
Lizzy: We already took that test, right?
Lizzy: Like it was the same exact test we took yesterday?
Barb: What?
Juniper: ...
Lizzy: And you said that yesterday too.
Barb: “What” is a reflexive response to you at this point.
Lizzy: No, the eons thing.
Lizzy: I thought it was a bit much then too.
Barb: Are you high or something?
Lizzy: Honestly, I have no idea.
Lizzy: Maybe.
join Noah midright [animation="Slide From Right" length="1.0" wait="true"]
Noah: Whoa, you’re high? That’s badass.
Barb: Of course you’d be interested in doing recreational drugs.
Barb: Your brain is already scrambled eggs.
Lizzy: Noah.
Lizzy: Tell me I’m not crazy and that today was yesterday.
Noah: ...
Noah: Uh. Sorry, what do you want me to say?
VO: This is just like the time I was in an alternate universe
VO: where I never got bit by the mayor
VO: and everyone was miserable because vampires were hanging out everywhere.
VO: Well, maybe this isn’t anything like that,
VO: but I’m feeling about the same as I did then.
- Tell everyone about the time you got transported[br]into an alternate universe where you were[br]never bitten and turned into a werewolf[br]and it was horrible and vampires hung out everywhere.
	Lizzy: Do you guys remember that time
	Lizzy: I got transported to an alternate universe where I was never turned into a werewolf
	Lizzy: and vampires were hanging out everywhere?
	Noah: I don’t personally remember, because I didn’t go to that alternate universe, but I remember you telling us about it.
	Barb: I’m still not sure I believe you.
	Juniper: ...
	VO: I should talk to Val, she’ll believe me! She’s got to.
	Lizzy: I’ve gotta go.
	Noah: Me too. Not for any suspicious reason or anything, this just feels like a natural conversation end point.
	Barb: Why am I even friends with you??


- Find an elegant way to leave the conversation[br]without suspicion because what if[br]you’re actually being mind probed by Lady MacDeath[br]and she’s trying to learn valuable secrets?
	Lizzy: I’m glad that we are good enough friends that I can leave a conversation without anyone thinking it’s weird.
	Barb: ....
